// input: after idr-optimize
// FILECHECK-OPTIONS: --implicit-check-not=@Main.iter(
// One copy of iter per static function argument: iter is partial, but its
// calls are not closed (n comes from stdin), so each is specialized on the
// constructor of the function sum it passes, which is in the key; a copy's
// name is iter's, its kind (`spec`) and its key's hash. The original iter is dead and
// removed. Each copy computes with its own function, in either order (two
// copies with the same function would share one key, so they would be one
// copy).
// CHECK: idr.func @Main.iter.spec.{{[^(]+}}(
// CHECK: arith.{{addi|muli}}
// CHECK: idr.func @Main.iter.spec.{{[^(]+}}(
// CHECK: arith.{{addi|muli}}
